{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535506-fate-of-fanum-and-local-gaoru","id":1535506,"title":"Fate of Fanum and local gaoru","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-13T01:18:38-07:00","id":1535506,"title":"Fate of Fanum and local gaoru","content":"Currently I'm working on small campaign around Chicago. OP supplement for VtM is sufficient for me to use it as general city outline\u200b. Fanum location and some places around are important in campaign but the most important is Fanum and information\u200b about garou in W5 (Including things from Book of Hungry Names).<br /> And so what do You think about the fate of Fanum? Please post any ideas.<br /> Here's my initial idea. Fanum was abandoned long time ago, nobody from local garou can exactly say why and when. No one can say what happened to Elders involved in Chicago war. From former Uktena to Shadow Lords, there's no sign about it. The main plot of adventure is to awake the Fanum caern once more, find some elders or information about them, learn from the past.<br /> But there's more. The first adventure will begin with some hunter who barely survived against member of Cult of Fenris and have been found and taken barely alive to local hospital. Local Glass Walker came across park monitoring and he's doing his best to keep the Veil and cover the tracks of crinos mauling some guy. The problem is that the hunter was a pawn of Abraham DuSable and that Tremere isn't going to be happy about the situation.<br /> The next problem is a guest from Green sept - I'm going to use Zachary Elison to subtly rebel local garou against each other to enter the stage as peacekeeper and one and only leader of Chicago tribes.<br /> Third problem if Fenrir who are watching from affair only to enter and strike against players to take control of Fanum and use it as a base for Chicago operations.<br /> Fourth problem are the Black Spiral Dancer who survived Chicago war and is waiting for perfect moment for revenge.<br /> <br /> I'm asking You to share any ideas what would happen to the Fanum and the elders and to share any ideas to expand the plot. \\<br /> <br /> Thank You.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-13T14:27:09-07:00","id":1535530,"title":"","content":"If I understand the backstory of the Fanum from Under a Blood Red Moon correctly, that area was originally &quot;just&quot; an Anchorhead - a gateway to the Deep Umbra. It didn't appear to actually be a caern. After the founding of Chicago in 1833 and the arrival of vampires into the area, Uktena kinfolk build the Fanum over the Anchorhead to protect it. However, when the Uktena used the Anchorhead to summon powerful spirits to protect them around 1871 from the European tribes, they inadvertently summoned an Incarna of the Celestine Jupiter that caused a lot of environmental and psychic turmoil. In order to prevent more chaos, the Uktena allied with Stargazers and Children of Gaia to recall Jupiter, but the improvised ritual did not send it back to the Deep Umbra, but became trapped in the building causing it to become a fetish of some source (which probably means that while the Incarna was sent back, some remnant as a jaggling avatar remained behind). Either because of this, or subsequent to this, the Fanum became a level 3 caern of Gnosis with Jupiter as its totem.<br /> <br /> So one possibility is that eventually the trapped Jupiter spirit simply went back home to the Deep Umbra causing the caern to disappear.<ul><li>Maybe this was a natural result given enough time after the original rite the Uktena, Stargazers, and Children of Gaia did.</li> <li>Maybe it was done on purpose by the sept of the Fanum as a result of seeing what happened during the events of Under a Blood Red Moon. They felt the possibility of Jupiter becoming corrupted as a result of it being trapped at the Fanum was too dangerous, and they purposefully did something to banish the spirit back to the Deep Umbra even though it meant the ending of the caern. Because this could be interpreted as violating a caern, this was kept secret.</li> <li>Another possibility is that this was inadvertent. Maybe the actual building of the Fanum became damaged and stopped being a fetish, and the incarna simply left. Maybe there was some kind of renovation, or a construction crane for a nearby building, had an accident that damaged the Fanum, or similar.</li> </ul>In this case, maybe it's possible the caern can be revived because of lingering spiritual energies, but the Fanum would get a brand new totem and perhaps become a different caern type.<br /> <br /> Another thing from UBRM is that neaeby the Fanum is the Orthodox Temple of Akhenaten which was built by the mummy Ilhaun (&quot;John Peabody&quot;) who assisted the sept of the Fanum in exchange for them protecting that building after his current body &quot;died&quot; until he came back. Maybe the mummy finally came back, and he is the reason for the Fanum is no longer around. Maybe he learned something during his underworld stay and came back to warn the Garou which cause the sept to leave the caern for reason unknown (but which you will determine). In this case maybe the caern still exists but inactive, but is somehow booby trapped to protect it. Perhaps the mummy's mortal servants now own or govern the Fanum, waiting for its true owners to come back (which might be never). But the other Garou have no way of knowing this was some deal, and if the mummy's servants explain it, they won't be believed. However, the mummy's servants have found a good way to protect the Fanum against the Black Spiral Dancers. Unfortunately, those same defenses work against uncorrupted Garou.<br /> <br /> There's lots of other ideas you can use, but these two pull directly from what we know about the Fanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-13T23:24:51-07:00","id":1535544,"title":"","content":"You enlightened me a lot. I forgot about the mummy, and the older history of Fanum, Thank You for deep research. Now I know that the plot will be smoke and mirrors type, cause I'm going to use all of it, of course most of them it will be false or half-truth but it should drive the players to chase the cluses.<br /> <br /> BTW Second question: In 2ed in Sept of Green Elison he tried to get on his side some garou. With who he could have succeeded? Spotlight? Simon Gentle?.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1784,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","user":"werewolf43","date":". 05-14-2024, 03:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-14T23:04:34-07:00","id":1535615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535506-fate-of-fanum-and-local-gaoru?p=1535544#post1535544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW Second question: In 2ed in Sept of Green Elison he tried to get on his side some garou. With who he could have succeeded? Spotlight? Simon Gentle?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you go by the description of the Sept of the Green in 1e/2e Werewolf corebook, almost everyone who is not a Bone Gnawer should want to depose Mother Larissa as the sept elder. Moots are held inconsistently. Only one moot per year is seriously planned, and the rest are disorganized. There is a 50 year agreement with the Sabbat vampires. Any traditional Garou is likely to be outraged. Spotlight should be an ally of Zachary unless given a very strong motive not to be by the ST. However, the traditional Garou do not dominate the Sept of the Green. The Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers do.<br /> <br /> The Glass Walkers are divided between Kleon and Harold. So most likely Zachary has gained the allegiance of any Garou not of the Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers, and is trying to see if either Kleon or Harold is willing to back him. Most likely Harold is the one most likely to make a deal. The Bone Gnawers will most likely rally around Mother Larissa, so for Zachary to succeed, he needs the support of the Glass Walkers which means he needs his ally Harold to win. If not, Mother Larissa will remain sept elder.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T01:25:12-07:00","id":1535620,"title":"","content":"I have similar point of view. After reading 5ed I take a stand that the Elders failed somehow but they wasn't wiped out from the map. Some of them lost the wolf, some lurks in the shadows trying to survive, some wait in the shadows for better times and some of them like Elison try to climb the ladder in new reality (nobody sa I can't use npc from older editions). So I have to assume that he left the Sept with his new/old formed pack including Spotlight, that teh discovered abandoned and unactive caern - Fanum and try to take it but carefuly. So first he's going to use players to discover truths about caern, push them to activate it and take it by force immediately after the proper rite. But there will be other factions involved that complicate plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}